  "about": "Car Lights' lamps by hand (src/car_lights.cpp, docs/graphics_effects.md#car-lights). Each car's list replaces the lamps found on its body, kind by kind (a list with only headlamps keeps the found tail lamps). Keys: rush2:<type 0-21>, rush2049:<car 0-12>, rush2049dc:<car 0-12>, calspeed:<car 0-20>, mod:<car name>, and <car key>/<livery file stem> for a livery. Positions in feet in the car's own axes (x across, y up, z forward), size the lens's radius in feet; the brightest texels within it glow as the lens or, with \"color\": [r, g, b] (the lens color pick measures), the texels near that color (\"lens\": false for a hidden lamp or a car without any, such as an open-wheel racer). tools/car_lamps.py pick measures an entry from a dump, and sheet --table draws every car with these over its lamps to check them.",
